BASIC BASH MANAGEMENT
pwd	: Shows current directory
ls	: Lists files and folders
ls -l	: Shows detailed list
ls -a	: Shows hidden files
ls -lh	: Shows file sizes in readable format
date	: Displays date and time
clear	: Clears terminal
cd : folder	Enters a folder
cd .. : 	Goes one directory back
cd ../.. :	Goes two directories back
cd ~ : 	Goes to home directory
cd /	: Goes to root directory
cd - : 	Goes to previous directory
mkdir : test	Creates a directory
rmdir : test	Removes an empty directory
touch file.txt :	Creates an empty file
cat file.txt: 	Displays file contents
cp a.txt b.txt :	Copies a file
mv a.txt b.txt: Renames or moves a file
rm file.txt	: Deletes a file





